## Implemented Contract

Classifier and request emission:

- First release creates one pending single; no eager request is emitted.
- Single emits only when elapsed is strictly greater than the configured
  interval. `T-epsilon`, `T`, and `T+epsilon` are distinct tested partitions.
- A recognized second press emits double immediately and suppresses the
  delayed single.
- Drag emits neither action. Ineligible frames pause emission, while document,
  scene, viewport, or explicit lifecycle reset clears stale physical intent.
- Pointer position and immutable viewport metrics are sampled at emission.
- Request construction binds current logical sample, physical attachment
  sample, projection/view/viewport identities, full P6-10 fence, occurrence
  generation, serial, intent, and normalized world ray.

Controller and effects:

- Terminal arrival is stored separately from commit. Ready heads commit in
  accepted serial order, one per caller update, so the caller can refresh the
  one selection authority context between commits.
- Out-of-order 3/1/2 completion, cancel/error head-of-line release,
  duplicate/unknown suppression, and lifecycle reset are covered.
- Every full fence field and occurrence generation participates in stale
  no-effect rejection.
- Single hit emits typed set/clear-capable exact-occurrence toggle and no-tab
  Browser reveal/scroll effects. Blank/current-invalid/hidden clears; stale,
  error, and cancellation do not overwrite newer state.
- Exact same `PrimitiveOccurrenceKey` always emits a clear-capable toggle,
  independent of the separate sole-highlight Node edge flag.
- Double hit emits finite camera center, positive speed, keep-eye, and exactly
  one view-revision successor. The modeled `[1,2,-2]` center and speed `5` are
  covered. Invalid/miss/stale/error/cancelled double results are no-ops.
- The controller stores no selection, camera, Browser, renderer, or UI
  authority; it emits immutable effects only.

Router and O06:

- One router owns classifier input, priority, capture, and batch terminal
  arbitration: modal, active/latched Gizmo, captured widget, picking, camera.
- DPI conversion consumes frozen `EditorViewportMetrics` once and preserves
  half-open boundaries at 100/125/150/200 percent scale.
- Gizmo capture remains owned outside viewport until delivered release or
  terminal detach/latch.
- A physical release is deferred until explicit frame close. Ordinary release
  with no Escape commits exactly once.
- O06 Escape/release in either same-batch order reaches the same clear,
  detach, release-capture, no-commit/no-history effect.
- O05 Escape-only is no-history. O07 focus loss latches retained preview with
  no manufactured commit. Late/repeated release cannot commit again.
- Prior-frame delivered ordinary release remains committed exactly once;
  later Escape does not retract or duplicate it.

